[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66777,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pleomorphic adenoma is a benign tumour with epithelial and modified myoepithelial cells intermingled with a chondromyxoid stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66778,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8940/0 Pleomorphic adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66779,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F00.Y &amp; XH2KC1 Other specified benign neoplasm of middle ear or respiratory system &amp; Pleomorphic adenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66780,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> benign mixed tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66781,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66782,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most pleomorphic adenomas arise in proximal bronchi or the trachea.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66783,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with endobronchial tumours may present with dyspnoea or haemoptysis, often associated with postobstructive pneumonia and/or atelectasis {26645458}. Intraparenchymal tumours are frequently asymptomatic. Imaging shows well-circumscribed solid masses {17670335; 11383642}. The heterogeneity of CT and MRI corresponds to different histological elements. Tumours may be PET-positive {11383642}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66784,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pleomorphic adenoma occurs within an age range of 8&ndash;74&nbsp;years {16863832}, but mostly in adults. There is no sex predominance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66785,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66786,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Reports of molecular studies in pulmonary pleomorphic adenomas are rare {9677459}, without documentation yet of the <em>PLAG1</em> and/or <em>HMGA2</em> fusions known to occur in salivary gland counterparts {28796899}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66787,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>Pleomorphic adenoma ranges from 10 to 160 mm {26645458}. Endobronchial pleomorphic adenoma is polypoid; parenchymal tumours are well-circumscribed nodules. The cut surface is white-grey, myxoid, and soft to rubbery.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-02T10:53:13"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66788,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Pulmonary pleomorphic adenomas are histologically similar to pleomorphic adenomas in salivary glands. They have a prominent tubular or ductal component associated with spindled to plasmacytoid myoepithelial cells embedded in a chondromyxoid stroma. Squamous metaplasia may also be seen {26645458}. Solid islands of epithelial cells with a focal myxoid stroma can be seen. Immunohistochemistry is not specific but supports a biphasic tumour. A panel of cytokeratin, S100, GFAP, p40, p63, calponin, &alpha;-SMA, and SMMHC will be variably positive. The key differential diagnosis is a metastatic salivary gland tumour (so-called benign metastasizing pleomorphic adenoma). Other differential diagnoses include pulmonary hamartoma and carcinosarcoma. Hamartomas comprise well-developed mesenchymal elements. Pulmonary carcinosarcomas have overtly malignant elements. Exceptionally, a malignancy may arise within a pleomorphic adenoma. The carcinoma component can be epithelial, myoepithelial, or mixed in origin and shows malignant features including necrosis, cellular atypia, &ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mitoses/2&nbsp;mm<sup>2</sup>, and vascular and/or perineural invasion. These tumours should be called carcinoma ex pleomorphic adenoma, and the type of carcinoma should be reported {26645458}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66789,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Although not reported in the pulmonary system, the finding of a combination of bland ductal epithelial cells and myoepithelial cells blended intimately with a chondromyxoid stroma would be expected.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66790,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66791,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>A benign mixed salivary gland&ndash;type neoplasm with ductal cells, myoepithelial cells, and a chondromyxoid stromal component</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-18T17:02:56"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66792,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66793,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 57,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Small, well-circumscribed tumours are benign. Tumours with infiltrative borders may recur and metastasize, and they behave as low-grade malignancies {22031319}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-11-11T12:01:42"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]